.\" Manpage for nornd (groff -man)
.\" View with: man -l contrib/man/nornd.8
.TH NORND 8 "2026-05-16" "norn-rs 0.3" "norn-rs Manual"
.SH NAME
nornd \- norn-rs mesh overlay daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nornd
[\fI\-c CONFIG\fR]
.br
.B nornd genconfig
[\fI\-o OUTPUT\fR]
.br
.B nornd showaddr
[\fI\-c CONFIG\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nornd
runs a node in the norn-rs encrypted overlay mesh. Each node has a stable
Ed25519 identity and a corresponding deterministic IPv6 address in the
.B 200::/7
range. Traffic between nodes is end-to-end encrypted with X25519 + ML-KEM-768
(post-quantum hybrid) session keys; intermediate hops see only ciphertext.
.PP
The daemon optionally creates a TUN device so that arbitrary IPv6 traffic
addressed to other mesh participants is transparently routed through the overlay.
.PP
Onion routing wraps Traffic packets in N concentric AEAD layers so that no
single relay learns both endpoints; fixed-size cells prevent global passive
observers from correlating packets across hops by size.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR \fICONFIG\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fICONFIG\fR
Path to the TOML config file (default: \fI/etc/norn/norn.toml\fR). The
file MUST have mode 0o600 or stricter (no group/other access) because it
contains the node's private key; nornd refuses to start otherwise.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B genconfig [\-o OUTPUT]
Generate a fresh config with a random private key. Writes to \fIOUTPUT\fR
(mode 0600, O_EXCL — refuses to overwrite) or stdout if \fI\-o\fR is omitted.
.TP
.B showaddr [\-c CONFIG]
Print the pub key and 200::/7 address derived from the configured private key.
.SH CONFIG FORMAT
.PP
The TOML config supports:
.RS
.TP
.B private_key
64-char hex Ed25519 private key. KEEP THIS SECRET.
.TP
.B listen
Array of TCP listen URIs. Default: \fB["tcp://0.0.0.0:9001"]\fR.
.TP
.B peers
Array of static peer URIs to dial on startup.
.TP
.B tun_name
TUN interface name. Omit to disable kernel-side routing (routing-only mode).
.TP
.B admin_socket
Path to the admin UNIX socket. Default: \fI/var/run/norn.sock\fR.
.TP
.B multicast_enabled
Whether to discover LAN peers via UDP multicast. Default: \fBtrue\fR.
.TP
.B multicast_port
UDP port for multicast beacons. Default: \fB9001\fR.
.TP
.B log_level
One of \fIerror\fR / \fIwarn\fR / \fIinfo\fR / \fIdebug\fR / \fItrace\fR.
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Overrides log filter (e.g. \fBnorn_rs=debug\fR). Takes precedence over the
\fIlog_level\fR config setting.
.TP
.B NORN_ALLOW_EPHEMERAL_KEY
If set to \fI1\fR, nornd starts without a configured private key by
generating a fresh ephemeral one each run. The node's identity and IPv6
address change every restart. Do NOT use this in production; the default
policy refuses ephemeral keys to avoid silent identity churn.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/norn/norn.toml
Default config path.
.TP
.I /var/run/norn.sock
Default admin UNIX socket.
.TP
.I /dev/net/tun
TUN device (requires \fBCAP_NET_ADMIN\fR or root).
.SH SECURITY
The config file holds the node's long-term Ed25519 private key. nornd
refuses to load a config with group- or world-readable permissions. The
admin socket is created with mode 0o600 atomically (umask narrowed before
\fBbind\fR(2) to close the TOCTOU window).
.PP
See SECURITY.md in the source distribution for the full threat model.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean shutdown (SIGTERM / Ctrl-C).
.TP
.B 1
Configuration or startup error (also: refused to load a permissive config).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nornctl (8)
.SH BUGS
Report security issues per SECURITY.md. Functional issues to the project
tracker.
